# Client data never belongs in this repository.
#
# The site is served by GitHub Pages from the repository root, and the repo
# is public — anything committed here is published twice over: once on the
# website and once through GitHub itself. Registers built from the Salesforce
# export (data/build-vehicle-register.py) are for importing into the PRIVATE
# Claims TT Google Sheet only.
data/*.csv
data/*.json

node_modules/
__pycache__/

# Worktrees the Claude Code harness creates for parallel build agents. Live
# scaffolding, never source: committing one would bring a second copy of the
# repository into the repository.
.claude/worktrees/

# Film build artefacts. The narration, the beds, the capture and the mix are
# all reproducible from tools/film/*-lines.json and *-timing.json, and they
# run to tens of megabytes each. The repository keeps the recipe, not the
# intermediate products — the MP4 and its poster are committed because the
# site serves them.
tools/film/vo*/
tools/film/cap*/
tools/film/_track.wav
tools/film/bed-*.wav
tools/film/sfx-*.wav
tools/film/*-mix.wav
tools/film/captions-*.ass

# the transition send: the departed agents' names and every client file stay out
tools/letters/departed.txt
tools/letters/exclude.txt
tools/letters/*.csv

# tools/ads intermediate: each poster's HTML embeds the font as base64 and is
# regenerated by build-ad.py in a second. The JPEGs beside the pages are the
# deliverable.
tools/ads/out/

# Film render intermediates. The pipeline in tools/film/ regenerates every one
# of these from the lines, the timing file and the builder, so none belongs in
# git — and the repository root is served by GitHub Pages, so a captured frame
# directory would be published as well as cloned. 1.4 GB of them at the last
# count. The finished MP4, its poster and the committed source track are
# tracked as normal; these are the scaffolding.
#   cap-<key>/      frame captures from render.js
#   vo<key>/        the voice WAVs and VTT cues importvox.py writes
#   *.wav           the beds, sound design and mixes
#   captions-*.ass  the burned-in caption script
tools/film/cap-*/
tools/film/vo*/
tools/film/*.wav
tools/film/captions-*.ass
